<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Vindhya Pradesh</h1><p class="st-meta">1948 CE – 1956 CE · capital Rewa</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The union of the Bundelkhand and Baghelkhand princely states, a short-lived Indian state with its capital at Rewa.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1948 the 35 states of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelkhand">Bundelkhand</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/rewa-state">Baghelkhand</a> agencies, among them Rewa, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/panna-state">Panna</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/orchha-state">Orchha</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/datia-state">Datia</a> and many tiny estates, were merged into the United State of Vindhya Pradesh, with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> of Rewa, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martand-singh">Martand Singh</a>, as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajpramukh">Rajpramukh</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The union proved unstable, and in 1950 it was made a centrally administered Part C state, with some enclaves exchanged with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttar-pradesh">Uttar Pradesh</a>. It had a largely rural economy, many former princely estates and low literacy. Rewa served as capital, and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/datia-state">Datia</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/orchha-state">Orchha</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khajuraho">Khajuraho</a> lay within its borders.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/states-reorganisation-act-1956">States Reorganisation Act</a> Vindhya Pradesh was merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a> on 1 November 1956.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/vindhya-pradesh.jpg" alt="Vindhya Pradesh" width="320" height="387"><figcaption>Image: Superbenjamin this file: Furfur · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vindhya_Pradesh_in_India_(1951).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1948 C